{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-10-25T00:09:27.613Z","author":"harness:codex","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"codex","agent_model":"gpt-6.1-sol","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"74cfeef4f534f3b98c3259d0","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"gpt-6.1-sol","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"probe"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"replace","path":"/body","value":"Follow-up to #946.\n\n## Observed\n\nWhen another process has changed items since the last read, `pm context` rebuilds its persisted context-signal snapshot and returns correct, fresh output. It still emits:\n\n```\nwarning_details[1]{code,meaning,recovery_command,recovery_effect}:\n  context_signal_store_stale,The persisted context-signal snapshot did not match the authoritative cursor or item corpus and was rebuilt.,pm context,Re-read context and confirm the rebuilt snapshot is now fresh.\nwarnings[1]: context_signal_store_stale\n```\n\nThe recovery advice asks the agent to run `pm context` again. That second read returns the same content without the warning: 2.4–3.7 KB (~600–940 estimated tokens) spent only to clear a cache message. In a multi-agent tracker, where other writers change items between every read, this happens on most first reads of a session. Seen on 2026-10-25 in two independent trackers (a companion hub with 1,285 items and a package tracker), each time followed by a clean re-read.\n\n## Expected\n\nA cache that was detected stale and rebuilt successfully within the same call is not a condition the caller needs to act on. Either:\n\n- report it as informational metadata (for example `cache: { context_signals: \"rebuilt\" }` in the read receipt) instead of `warnings`, with no recovery command; or\n- keep a warning only when the rebuild failed or the output was produced from the stale snapshot.\n\nAgents treat `warnings` as something to act on, so a self-healed cache should not appear there.\n\nVersion: `@unbrained/pm-cli` 2026.10.24."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-gh1581"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"GH-1581: Report successful context snapshot refresh without recovery warnings"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"pm context reports a self-healed snapshot rebuild as a warning and recommends a redundant second read"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":2},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["agent-ux","context-management","gh:1581","sdk"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-10-25T00:09:27.613Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-10-25T00:09:27.613Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:codex"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":180},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"Successful stale-cache rebuild produces fresh context without redundant warning/re-read instruction; retain actionable warnings on failed persistence or corrupt data and observable refresh status."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-4k6b"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments","value":[{"created_at":"2026-10-25T00:09:27.613Z","author":"harness:codex","text":"Intake source: 1581. Duplicate check: complete strict 3101-item all-status corpus with no omissions, request-specific searches and current open/in_progress lists; related delivered lineage retained. Report recorded for independent verification. No implementation or completion claimed by intake."}]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/escape_class","value":"production_defect"}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"a07826b0272a3d1b31f0c8bb606458eac3b06e481a59211279c8e2